 (:calendar "NG" :key "decree-1979-3" :from (1979 1 1) :to nil
  :authority "Public Holidays Decree 1979 (Decree No. 3 of 1979)"
  :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20240616072641/https://archive.gazettes.africa/archive/ng/1979/ng-government-gazette-supplement-dated-1979-02-01-no-5.pdf"
  :issued (1979 1 17) :issued-uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20240616072641/https://archive.gazettes.africa/archive/ng/1979/ng-government-gazette-supplement-dated-1979-02-01-no-5.pdf" :published (1979 2 1) :published-uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20240616072641/https://archive.gazettes.africa/archive/ng/1979/ng-government-gazette-supplement-dated-1979-02-01-no-5.pdf" :published-in "Supplement to Official Gazette No. 5, Vol. 66, 1st February 1979 - Part A (pp. A5-A7)" :in-force (1979 1 1) :summary "s.1 days in the Schedule are public holidays throughout Nigeria; s.2(1) Head of FMG (now President) may by public notice appoint special days (s.2(3): incl. work-free days); s.3 Commissioner (Minister) for Internal Affairs may substitute another day; s.5(b) a holiday on Saturday or Sunday gets NO day in lieu; s.5(d) Sunday+Monday pair -> only the Monday. Schedule: New Year's Day, Good Friday, Easter Monday, National Day (1 Oct), Christmas Day, and 'such day as the Commissioner may declare' for Id el Fitr, Id el Kabir and Id el Maulud (one day each in the text). No Boxing Day in the Schedule.")
